===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|calcium carbonate rock}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} A soft, white, [[powdery]] [[limestone]] (calcium carbonate, CaCO<sub>3</sub>).
#: {{ux|en|'''chalk''' cliffs are not recommended for climbing}}
# {{senseid|en|chalkboard chalk}} {{lb|en|countable}} A piece of chalk, or nowadays processed compressed [[gypsum]] (calcium sulfate, CaSO{{sub|4}}), that is used for drawing and for writing on a [[blackboard]] ([[chalkboard]]).
#: {{ux|en|the '''chalk''' used to write on the blackboard makes a squeaky sound}}
# {{senseid|en|tailor's chalk}} [[tailor's chalk|Tailor's chalk]].
# {{senseid|en|gymnast's chalk}} {{lb|en|uncountable|climbing|gymnastics}} A white powdery substance used to prevent hands slipping from holds when climbing, or losing grip in weight-lifting or gymnastics, sometimes but not always limestone-chalk, often magnesium carbonate (MgCO<sub>3</sub>).
#: {{ux|en|when working out your next move, it's a good idea to get some more '''chalk''' from the bag}}
# {{senseid|en|airborne group}} {{lb|en|US|military|countable}} A [[platoon]]-sized group of [[airborne]] [[soldier]]s.
# {{senseid|en|favored athlete}} {{lb|en|US|sports|chiefly|basketball|horse racing}} The favorite in a sporting event.
# {{senseid|en|win by a favored athlete}} {{lb|en|US|sports|chiefly|basketball}} The prediction that there will be no upsets, and the [[favored]] competitor will win.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1982 March 22|author=Phil Musick|title=And the pick here is - Georgetown over Houston|journal=Pittsburgh Post-Gazette| url=http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=p-YNAAAAIBAJ&sjid=lG0DAAAAIBAJ&pg=5414,4919698| page=13| passage=OK, let's get rid of the '''chalk''' players right away. The '''chalk''' likes North Carolina. Dean Smith has taken Carolina to the Final Four six times.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=1995 April 6|title=Notes on a Scorecard|journal=Los Angeles Times|url=http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/latimes/access/22775635.xml?dids=22775635:22775635&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT|page=C3|passage=Excuse us for sticking with the '''chalk''', but the predicted winners are Afternoon Deelites in the Derby, Oliver McCall over Larry Holmes, Nick Faldo in the Masters, and Al Unser Jr. in the Grand Prix.|accessdate=19 March 2009|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120306021907/http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/latimes/access/22775635.xml?dids=22775635:22775635&FMT=ABS&FMTS=ABS:FT|archivedate=6 March 2012}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2008 March 24|author=Jason Bauman|title=Non-news of the week: Obama picks North Carolina|journal=Beacon-News|location=Aurora, Illinois| url=http://nl.newsbank.com/nl-search/we/Archives?p_text_direct-0=11FF7064C02E5360&p_field_direct-0=document_id| passage=Instead, he played the '''chalk''' and selected the No. 1 overall seed in the tournament.}}

