===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To apply chalk to anything, such as the tip of a [[billiard]] [[cue]].
#: {{ux|en|'''chalk''' your hands before climbing}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1944|month=January and February|author=Major J. C. F. Lloyd Williamson|title=Ambulance Trains in Algeria and Tunisia|journal=Railway Magazine|page=6|text=After a leg stretch, we set off again at 11:30 hours in charge of U.S.A. No. 1736 (''Miss Ohio'' had been '''chalked''' on her), a 2-8-0 utility engine.}}
# To record something, as on a [[blackboard]], using chalk.
# To use powdered chalk to mark the lines on a playing field.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} To record a score or event, as if on a chalkboard.
# To [[manure]] (land) with chalk.
#* {{RQ:Mortimer Husbandry|passage=Land that is '''chalked'''}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1821|author=Royal Society of Arts (Great Britain)|title=Transactions|volume=39|page=11|passage=I then '''chalked''' the land at an expense of 4''l.'' per acre, and planted potatoes, about ten bushels to the acre {{...}}}}
# To make white, as if with chalk; to make pale; to bleach.
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Princess|passage=Fear Stared in her eyes, and '''chalked''' her face}}
#* {{RQ:Herbert Temple
|passage=Let a bleak paleness '''chalk''' the door.}}

